# Schema / Connector Sync Rule

When the user adds or edits tables or columns in analyzer `schema.json`, or asks to sync a Fivetran connector:

## 1. Detect the delta

Identify affected tables:
- New table names in JSON
- New column names on existing tables
- Columns with crude types (`text`, `integer`, `numeric`, `boolean`, `timestamp`)
- Columns missing `type_confidence`
- Do **not** reprocess tables where all columns have `type_confidence` of `source`, `rule`, `ai`, or `ai_verified` unless the user explicitly asks

Preserve manual overrides: columns with `type_confidence: manual` must not be overwritten.

## 2. Run incremental analyser (not a full rerun)

Use the source-system-analyser API scripts. Paths are relative to the skill:

```bash
SKILL=./.cursor/skills/source-system-analyser
.venv/bin/python "$SKILL/scripts/apis/api_analyzer.py" \
  --discovery api_discovery.json \
  --data-dir ./api_data \
  --base-url "$API_BASE_URL" \
  --output schema_api.json \
  --merge-into schema_api.json \
  --detect-changes \
  --recommend-types snowflake \
  --verify-types \
  --fetch-live
```

Or for explicit tables:

```bash
  --tables stg_new_table \
  --recommend-types snowflake
```

Replace `snowflake` with the target dialect: `snowflake`, `sqlserver`, `postgresql`, or `oracle`.

## 3. Type enrichment checklist (when ambiguous types remain)

```bash
.venv/bin/python "$SKILL/scripts/apis/build_type_enrichment_checklist.py" \
  schema_api.json --dialect snowflake -o schema_type_checklist.json
```

Work the checklist table by table. For uncertain columns, fetch up to 10 live API rows before assigning `proposed_type`. Merge back:

```bash
.venv/bin/python "$SKILL/scripts/apis/apply_type_enrichment.py" \
  schema_api.json schema_type_checklist.json --in-place
```

## 4. Sync connector if it exists

If `connectors/<name>/connector.py` exists for this source:

```bash
.venv/bin/python "$SKILL/scripts/apis/sync_connector_schema.py" \
  schema_api.json connectors/dbt_cloud_logs/connector.py
```

Only update `schema()` — do not change `update()` unless the user asks.

## 5. Report changes

List:
- Tables/columns updated in `schema.json`
- Whether connector `schema()` was synced
- Any columns still pending in the type checklist

## Guardrails

- Never embed API tokens in commands; use env vars (`API_BEARER_TOKEN`, etc.)
- Do not full-rerun the analyser when only one table changed
- Do not overwrite `table_description`, `column_description`, classifications, or manual types on unchanged tables
